# Saaridge mediation guarantee

Read and obey [`CONSTRAINTS.md`](../../CONSTRAINTS.md) for this repo.

## Never do

- Add hostname/URL allowlists or static MITM passthrough entries (e.g. `linkedin.com`) to “fix” browsing.
- Soft-open container egress or re-enable host `terminal_exec`.
- Bypass [`host/bridge/control/lib.js`](../../host/bridge/control/lib.js) for host or network text the agent sees.
- Ship app- or agent-specific workarounds (named product trust paths, per-app passthrough, one-off launch hacks); use shared container/bridge mechanisms instead.

## Always preserve

- Host FS virtualization via Data API + control lib.
- Bridge-owned handling of `vault://` (lib → resolve → upstream → lib on response); never blind TUNNEL for vault markers.
- Encrypted vault at rest under `state/private/` (bridge-only).
- Fail-closed network lock (IPv4 + IPv6 + DNS pin).
- Adaptive (runtime) MITM passthrough only — no checked-in site lists. See `CONSTRAINTS.md`.
- Treat the **host operator as trusted** (ideal, non-malicious). Do not add complexity that only defends against a hostile host.
